cff-version: 1.2.0
type: dataset
message: >-
  Please cite this replication package and the accompanying paper when using
  these data or code, and acknowledge the OECD SWACHE project as the survey
  source. The data and questionnaire figures are licensed under CC BY 4.0;
  the R code is licensed separately under MIT.
title: >-
  The value of a statistical case of hypertension: Stated preference evidence
  from ten OECD countries — replication data and code
authors:
  - family-names: King
    given-names: Peter
    affiliation: "Institute for Transport Studies, University of Leeds, Leeds, UK"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8550-466X"
  - family-names: Hunt
    given-names: Alistair
    affiliation: "University of Bath, Bath, UK"
  - family-names: Holland
    given-names: Mike
    affiliation: "EMRC, UK"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pmpk20/Hypertension_VSC"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Survey data and R code for estimating willingness to pay to reduce
  hypertension risk and the value of a statistical case across ten OECD
  countries. Includes 12,182 completed responses, page timings, a codebook,
  and scripts and outputs for the paper and supplementary information.
  Data and questionnaire figures: CC BY 4.0. R code: MIT.
  The data support comparisons of willingness to pay across countries and
  alternative analyses of risk valuation, income effects and sample-screening
  rules.
keywords:
  - hypertension
  - willingness to pay
  - contingent valuation
  - stated preference
  - health economics
  - environmental economics
  - value of a statistical case
  - replication
  - R
  - OECD SWACHE
# Code: MIT (LICENSE). Data and questionnaire figures: CC BY 4.0 (Data/LICENSE.md).
